# The app builds its own private Python environment in here the first time it starts: about 1.5 GB of
# torch, napari and Qt, compiled for one operating system. The launcher rebuilds it in minutes on any
# machine, and it is not portable between machines even in principle, so it must never be committed.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS writes one of these into every folder it displays.
.DS_Store

# A SAFETY NET, NOT A NECESSITY. Nothing in this package is an image or a result, and package_app.py
# never copies one -- it ships the program and the model, and the data stays on the machine it was
# collected on. But this folder is a working copy of an app that reads sections and writes its counts
# beside them, so if a TIF or a "counted cells.csv" is ever dropped in here to try something out,
# these lines are what stop it being published. Unpublished data is the one mistake a repository
# cannot take back: GitHub and third parties cache and index what they have seen, so "I deleted it"
# does not undo it.
*.TIF
*.tif
*.tiff
*.csv
*.npz
*.xlsx
